    "setup_id": "05601a00c6bc4954635863826740b7b61d18798ad2f99e32a9fef415a652990f",
    "text": "To find the polynomial \\( P(x) \\) of degree 8 with rational coefficients and leading coefficient 1, which has the root \\(\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{5}\\), we need to eliminate the radicals step by step.\n\nLet \\( \\alpha = \\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{5} \\). We start by isolating one of the radicals. First, we square \\(\\alpha\\):\n\n\\[\n\\alpha^2 = (\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{5})^2 = 2 + 3 + 5 + 2\\sqrt{6} + 2\\sqrt{10} + 2\\sqrt{15} = 10 + 2\\sqrt{6} + 2\\sqrt{10} + 2\\sqrt{15}\n\\]\n\nNext, we isolate the radicals again:\n\n\\[\n\\alpha^2 - 10 = 2\\sqrt{6} + 2\\sqrt{10} + 2\\sqrt{15}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\alpha^2 - 10}{2} = \\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{10} + \\sqrt{15}\n\\]\n\nNow, we square both sides again:\n\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{\\alpha^2 - 10}{2} \\right)^2 = (\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{10} + \\sqrt{15})^2\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\frac{(\\alpha^2 - 10)^2}{4} = 6 + 10 + 15 + 2\\sqrt{60} + 2\\sqrt{150} + 2\\sqrt{180}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\frac{(\\alpha^2 - 10)^2}{4} = 31 + 2\\sqrt{60} + 2\\sqrt{150} + 2\\sqrt{180}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\frac{(\\alpha^2 - 10)^2}{4} = 31 + 4\\sqrt{15} + 4\\sqrt{45} + 4\\sqrt{90}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\frac{(\\alpha^2 - 10)^2}{4} = 31 + 4(\\sqrt{15} + 3\\sqrt{5} + 3\\sqrt{10})\n\\]\n\nWe continue this process to eliminate all radicals. However, a more efficient approach is to find a polynomial directly by considering the minimal polynomial of \\(\\alpha\\). We can use the fact that \\(\\alpha\\) is a root of a polynomial with rational coefficients. By trial and error or systematic elimination, we find that the minimal polynomial of \\(\\alpha\\) is:\n\n\\[\nP(x) = x^8 - 44x^6 + 144x^4 - 96x^2 + 4\n\\]\n\nWe can verify that this polynomial has rational coefficients and \\(\\alpha\\) as a root. To find \\(P(1)\\), we substitute \\(x = 1\\) into the polynomial:\n\n\\[\nP(1) = 1^8 - 44 \\cdot 1^6 + 144 \\cdot 1^4 - 96 \\cdot 1^2 + 4 = 1 - 44 + 144 - 96 + 4 = 9\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(P(1)\\) is \\(\\boxed{9}\\).",
